  message: "Done in PR #2176 (commit 84dde547ab). Re-ran the filed repro (this repository's sketch at 8k). The two lines that named no file now read:\n  `main` (Python main()) — `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py` — Primary CLI entry point.\n  `main` (Python main()) — `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/runtime_coherence.py` — CLI entry point. Returns exit code.\nRULE (reads the names shown, never a particular name or language): an entry whose displayed name another shown entry also carries shows its path as well as its docstring; two such entries in one file show path:line; a name shared only with an entry the section does not show is unique. A line says a thing once: an entry named by its own path does not repeat it, and a label drops the name or path it ends with.\nACCEPTANCE ON OTHER REPOSITORIES, 8k, same number of entries before and after: alertmanager (Go) 59 entries, 5135 -> 4509 chars, the three `New` exports each located (silence/silence.go, notify/pagerduty/pagerduty.go, notify/incidentio/incidentio.go) and four `main` each with its cmd path; kserve (Python and Go) 61 entries, 7012 -> 4953 chars. Fixture tests cover Go commands, JS handlers (one with a docstring, one without), a Rust name shared across two groups, and two TypeScript handlers in one file. Seven mutations each turned a test red.\nNOT DONE: a JS/TS repository with several same-named handlers was tested as a fixture, not on a real repository. Two route markers of one route in one file show path:line, which locates each and does not say how they differ. Seen while rendering, not fixed, to be filed: this repository's HTTP Routes list shows a raw symbol id as a route's handler (`POST /api/items` → `python:packages/...:_api_add_item:function`) and lists each route twice (once as the handler function, once as the route marker)."  # ed08
